<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John III, Duke of Cleves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1539">1539</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as John the Peaceful</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John III, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>, called the Peaceful, married Maria, heiress of Jülich and Berg. On inheriting from his father and father-in-law by 1521 he united Cleves, Mark, Jülich, Berg and Ravensberg into the United Duchies, a major power of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. He followed a humanist middle way in religion, and his daughter Anne married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII of England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-iii-duke-of-cleves.jpg" alt="John III, Duke of Cleves" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_III_von_Kleve-J%C3%BClich-Berg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1512, during the Italian Wars, Ferdinand the Catholic accused the Albret monarchs, <b>John III</b> and Catherine of Foix, of siding with France and sent the Duke of Alba to seize Pamplona.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1521 Duke <b>John III</b> united Cleves with Jülich and Berg, forming the United Duchies.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-cleves">Duchy of Cleves</a></li><li><blockquote><b>John III</b> of Cleves-Mark married Maria, heiress of Jülich, Berg and Ravensberg.</blockquote><a href="/state/united-duchies-of-julich-cleves-berg">United Duchies of Jülich-Cleves-Berg</a></li></ul></section>
